{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_iii", "label": "Article III \u2014 Evidence and interpretation are distinct", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "label": "Stage 15 \u2014 Topics (implemented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A topic is a judgment about a claim, so it must be a signed, attributable, challengeable log entry rather than a column someone edits. The vocabulary is closed and two levels deep so filing is checkable, and each node names the audit/reputation domain it maps to so reputation stays per subject without a second vocabulary. Untagged claims stay in `general` rather than being unscorable (conservative reading)."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_tag_claim", "label": "TAG_CLAIM epistemic contribution", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filing is a judgment, so it is a signed contribution projected to `claim_topics` with validity windows: auto-accepted only for the claim's own principal, PENDING as a proposal on someone else's claim, superseded deterministically at apply time by a later tag from the same principal. Unknown paths are TOPIC_UNKNOWN; a delegation may restrict `permissions.topics`."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_topic_vocabulary", "label": "config/topics.yml closed topic vocabulary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Twelve top-level subjects with children, each naming the audit/reputation domain it maps to; kept as data rather than code so filing never invents a subject. Adding a topic stays a code change for now (reserved decision)."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_topics_backfill", "label": "topics:backfill \u2014 system-signed guessed tags", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Guesses are recorded as system-signed TAG_CLAIM entries whose note says they are guesses, and REPLACE=1 re-guesses only earlier backfills, never tags set by people or assistants, so a machine guess can never quietly overwrite a human judgment."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_optional_page_hash", "label": "Optional page hash for a source held by reference", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hosted assistants (claude.ai) see rendered text, not page bytes, so Claude rightly refused to invent a content_hash and recorded nothing. What Galedra verifies for such a source is the quoted excerpt with its own hash, the link and the time of reading; tools now say to omit the hash rather than fabricate it. Article II still holds."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_say_instead", "label": "Say-instead line, short and plain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A supported claim is itself what to say, so a say-instead line is offered only when the claim as stated does not hold up; a candidate over 25 words is skipped rather than cut short, so the line is a whole graph sentence or absent. Nothing is composed or paraphrased (Invariant 10)."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_purpose_before_plumbing", "label": "Purpose before plumbing (three things a person does with Galedra)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asked what Galedra is for, Claude listed ten tools and their enums. The initialize instructions and the skill now open with the three uses; an empty search returns the total of accepted claims plus a note that the subject is more likely unrecorded than mis-searched, because Claude could not tell an empty ledger from a narrow search."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_anonymous_consent", "label": "One plugin, the person decides (anonymous or attributed consent)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The consent page no longer requires sign-in up front; an anonymous grant issues a fresh anonymous assistant key per grant, adoptable later, so one /mcp/connect plugin serves both attributed and anonymous use and reinstalling to switch is never needed."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_chatgpt_interop", "label": "ChatGPT connector interop fixes (OpenID discovery, RFC 9207, plain form submit)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Found by watching the log: ChatGPT fetches /.well-known/openid-configuration first, requires authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported and client_id_metadata_document_supported, and verifies iss before exchanging a code (RFC 9207); the consent form was submitted by Turbo, which cannot follow a cross-site redirect, so approvals went nowhere until it became a plain page submission."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_tag_claim", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_topic_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_topics_backfill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_optional_page_hash", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_say_instead", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-15-topics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_15_topics_purpose_before_plu